+### Fix
+
+Use `SafeERC20` for the approval as well as the transfer, and use the
+force-approve form, because USDT additionally refuses to move a non-zero allowance
+to another non-zero value:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`SafeERC20.forceApprove` (OpenZeppelin >= 4.9, already a dependency here) resets the
+allowance to zero first and tolerates missing return data. Do not reach for
+`safeApprove` — it is deprecated and reverts on a non-zero-to-non-zero change.
+
+While you are there, audit every other external token call for the same problem.
+In this contract that is the complete list, but the rule to adopt is "no bare
+`IERC20` calls on USDT, ever."
+
